 By month's end the tunnels under Pyrmont, Balmain East, and the long loop beneath the Barangaroo foreshore and Hickson Road have emptied. The Burrows are yours to inhabit. Above ground the rough sleeper count has visibly risen, fresh bodies around the Anzac Bridge approaches and under the overpasses where there were none the week before. That is somebody else's problem. What you have built down here is a new kind of territory, unlit, unclaimed by any Regent, and waiting.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":2,"response":"The Siphon is a large chamber and it is mostly empty when you start. You spend the first week moving your possessions down through the service tunnels, the coffin, the ledgers, the pieces that matter. The second week is the vitae work. You shed blood into the corners and the blood holds the shape you want it to hold; the space begins to exhale wrongness. You engineer the approaches so that anyone who comes down the wrong corridor hears distant screaming before they hear footsteps, and the screaming is not yours. By the third week the Burrows around your new lair behave themselves without you having to patrol them; the space has acquired a reputation the rats pass on to each other. By the end of the month you sleep here. Safe Place now in the Under-Harbour.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":3,"response":"The apparatus hums across the month. Networks maintained, new members grooming, resources allocated, the occasional small fire put out before it could become a large one. The North Shore arm in particular is in the best shape it has been in. A corrupt hat full of deplorable arseholes. Tasty arseholes. Xavier's arrival mid-cycle has tightened what you had already built in ways you might have resented from anyone else, and from Xavier you recognise as correction you needed.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"general_notes":"Test","locked":true,"resource_approvals":[null,null,null,null,null,null,{"action_index":6,"approved":true,"flag_note":"","reviewed_by":"Angelus"}]},"acquisitions_resolved":[{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"If people investigate the area it will look like a Safe Place +3","created_at":"2026-04-16T11:35:54.850Z"}],"story_context":"If people investigate the area it will look like a Safe Place +3","pool_validated_by":"Von Vagabond"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"I'm sure the real-world tech is very cool; but can you please let us know what piece of equipment from one of the books you want (Chronical of Darkness or Hurt Locker) or it will just be a very nice camera.","pool_validated_by":"Von Vagabond"}],"feeding_roll_player":{"cols":[{"r":{"v":5,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":5,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":1,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":4,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]}],"successes":3,"vessels":3,"safeVitae":6,"methodName":"Other","pool":9,"again":9,"breakdown":"ST confirmed: Presence 4 + Empathy 4 = 8 + Motives +1 — 9-Again","rolledAt":"2026-04-17T08:11:49.869Z","dramaticFailure":false},"feeding_deferred":null,"feeding_vitae_allocation":[2,2,2],"feeding_vitae_tally":{"herd":5,"ambience":3,"ambience_territory":"North Shore","oath_of_fealty":0,"ghouls":0,"rite_cost":0,"manual":0,"total_bonus":8}},{"_id":"69da37d0cc5483a3c77027a1","cycle_id":"69d0a3c5052b57f6be774e69","character_id":"69d73ea49162ece35897a47c","character_name":"Alice Vunder","player_name":"Katherine Honan","status":"submitted","timestamp":"9/04/2026 0:43","attended":true,"_raw":{"submission":{"timestamp":"9/04/2026 0:43","email":"honankatherine@gmail.com","player_name":"Katherine Honan","character_name":"Alice Vunder","attended_last_game":true},"narrative":{"travel_description":"I can't remember the entire answer I wrote but it involved getting lost a lot. It was something like taking the wrong train and getting off at the wrong station and having to catch a train back to where I was meant to go and then still getting lost","game_recount":"Helped Anichka with braiding her red ribbons. They made her think of red ribbons of blood in the water.\nSaw a fight at the club when went dancing with cyrus. Instantly went to help Kindred and keep the masquerade intact.\nTried to bargain with Conrad for regency but he just insulted all crones, then afterwards said he was only trying to shield another territory and offered a boon to Alice. She accepted it.\nBecame regent without much warning\nChatted with Renee about how keeper can mess with memories, then realised alice doesn't remember bits from the party with cyrus","standout_rp":"Conrad, for being a religious shit. Anichka, for helping Alice realise that she is struggling with the anger of the beast.","ic_correspondence":"I had an email alice sent to her family that was about the new club and how she is now in a new position and feels very nervous about it and also that all these people at the new club talking about bringing in the old ways and the old people made her feel protective of her home country","most_trusted_pc":"anichka, brandy, tegan, maybe cryus","actively_harming_pc":"Conrad. but not in a way where alice would endanger herself or get caught.","aspirations":"same as before"},"regency":{"is_regent":true,"territory":"The North Shore","residency_grants":["Alice Vunder","Preacher Willows","Brandy LaRoux","Yusuf the Carthian","Balls the Invictus"],"total_residency_count":5,"regency_action":"This is not a place to bring the old world to and impose old ways upon. This territory is its own entity, and must be respected as such."},"feeding":{"method":"Primary Feeding Pool: Intelligence + Stealth \nBlood Type: Human\nFeeding Style: Hangs out near the Ivy club and feeds on a guy trying to pressure a far too drunk girl to go home with him.","territories":{"The Academy":"Not feeding here","The Harbour":"Not feeding here","The Dockyards":"Not feeding here","The Second City":"Not feeding here","The North Shore":"Resident","The Barrens (No Territory)":"Not feeding here"}},"influence":{"The Academy":0,"The Harbour":0,"The Dockyards":0,"The Second City":0,"The Shore":1},"projects":[{"action_type":"patrol_scout","action_type_raw":"Patrol/Scout: Attempt to monitor a given Territory or area 👀","primary_pool":{"expression":"Presence 3 + Socialise 2 + Contact street 3 = 8","size":8},"secondary_pool":{"expression":"NA","size":null},"desired_outcome":"Keep the Shore safe","description":"Project Name: Keeping it Tight! (Alice version, credit to Jack)\nCharacters Involved: Me (and Preacher Willows (Leo T), Brandy LaRoux (Ash), Ivana Horvat (Lyn H), Balls the Invictus)\nMerits & Bonuses:\nXp Spend: n/a\nProject Description: \nThe Shore is actively patrolled to keep out poachers or interlopers, and to reinforce the Masquerade with the Great Unwashed. Let it be known by all that Court has been established, and a Regent chosen for this district who watches from every shadow. Kindred may pass through, quickly and without stopping -- but pause for too long at your peril!","project_name":"Keeping it Tight! (Alice version, credit to Jack)","characters":null,"xp_spend":"n/a","merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters Involved: Me (and Preacher Willows (Leo T), Brandy LaRoux (Ash), Ivana Horvat (Lyn H), Balls the Invictus)\nMerits & Bonuses:\nProject Description: \nThe Shore is actively patrolled to keep out poachers or interlopers, and to reinforce the Masquerade with the Great Unwashed. Let it be known by all that Court has been established, and a Regent chosen for this district who watches from every shado